<p align="left" class="body1"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-22 | Monday</font></strong><br/><br/><span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-family: Times; font-size: 16px"><div align="justify"><span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 15px"><p style="margin-top: 0px; margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 13px; margin-left: 0px; line-height: 20px; font: normal normal normal 13px/normal Verdana; color: #333333"><span class="Apple-style-span" style="color: #000000; font-family: Arial; font-size: 12px; line-height: 15px">Peace to <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">Tone</span> and <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">Trevz</span> at <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://thenewpop.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">THENEWPOP.COM</a> for documenting our daytime excursions through New York City's Lower East Side and ending in Brooklyn. What happens when two dudes from Seattle visit New York City to ask The People (people = hip-hop heads, DJs, leftist bookstore staff, clothing designers, barbershop dwellers) their opinion on the topic of police brutality? FInd out at thenewpop.com very soon. We'll let you know when the episode is up. Peace to DV One! And don't forget...</span></p><p style="margin-top: 0px; margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 13px; margin-left: 0px; line-height: 20px; font: normal normal normal 13px/normal Verdana; color: #333333"><span class="Apple-style-span" style="color: #000000; font-family: Arial; font-size: 12px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 15px">October 22: <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: normal">a </span><a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://seattle.craigslist.org/see/pol/450410885.html" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: normal">National Day of Protest against Police Brutality</span></a><span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: normal">. Wear Black.</span></span></p></span></div></span><blockquote><span class="Apple-style-span" style="color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px; text-align: justify"><span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-style: italic">“October 22nd has come to be recognized as a concentrated day of resistance -- a national day when people all over the country, in different cities and through different means of expression, come together to STOP police violence, repression, and the criminalization of a generation. The nationwide epidemic of police brutality and repression is hidden from many people who would be outraged if they knew what was happening. We must resist the onslaught of police abuse as we work in many different ways to drag this truth out into the light of day. Our resistance will give others courage…”</span></span><br/></blockquote><blockquote style="text-align: justify"><span class="Apple-style-span" style="color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px"><br/></span></blockquote><blockquote style="text-align: justify"><span class="Apple-style-span" style="color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px"><br/></span></blockquote><p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-17 | Wednesday</font></strong><br/><br/><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal"><span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-style: italic">*Note: Flyer above originally posted in March</span></p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal"> </p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">After a year of delays, <span class="Apple-style-span" style="font-weight: bold">DV One's</span> trial begins today (Wednesday, October 17th) at the King County Courthouse. (If you've been out of the loop, sleeping under a rock, or just not paying attention for the past year - <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://slog.thestranger.com/2006/09/dj_dvone_attacked_by" rel="noopener noreferrer">your final late pass</a>.) </p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal; min-height: 13px"> </p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Two weeks ago, the Seattle Police Department's Office of Professional Accountability (OCA) <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://slog.thestranger.com/2007/10/dvones_opa_complaint" rel="noopener noreferrer">cleared the officers</a> who arrested DV of any wrongdoing. Many versions of the story exist. But all of them end the same way: with an unarmed DV One beaten and tased. Plus, it's happened to many others many times before. </p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal; min-height: 13px"> </p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Just as DV himself said outside his first pre-trial hearing, this is bigger than just him. It could have been you or me. And it can still be. Unless we let em know we're not having it. Stand up for DV and ourselves.</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal"> </p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">King County Superior Court</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">516 3rd Ave</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Courtroom W-817</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal"> </p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Trial will be in session on the following days:</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal"> </p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Wednesday, October 17, 2007 9am</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Thursday, October 18, 2007 9am</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Friday – NO COURT</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Monday, October 22, 2007 9am</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Tuesday, October 23, 2007 9am</p><p style="margin: 0px; font-family: Verdana; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-weight: normal; font-size: 11px; line-height: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-stretch: normal">Wednesday, October 24, 2007 9am</p><p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-12 | Friday</font></strong><br/><br/><p class="massline-embed-gap">Archived embedded media is unavailable for offline playback. <a class="massline-external-playback" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hm3lbUwcmg8" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open video hm3lbUwcmg8 on YouTube (external playback)</a></p>

man, the jerk chicken at that restaurant was so disappointing.  bring back the pho.<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-10 | Wednesday</font></strong><br/><br/><strong>TOMORROW NIGHT:</strong><br><br><img alt="Archived image unavailable"><br><br><font size="2"><a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://msplinks.com/MDFodHRwOi8vd3d3Lm15c3BhY2UuY29tL2RqdmFkaW0=" rel="noopener noreferrer">DJ Vadim</a><br><a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://msplinks.com/MDFodHRwOi8vd3d3Lm15c3BhY2UuY29tL2Fic3RyYWN0cnVkZQ==" rel="noopener noreferrer">Abstract Rude</a><br><a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://msplinks.com/MDFodHRwOi8vd3d3Lm15c3BhY2UuY29tL3lhcmFoYnJhdm8=" rel="noopener noreferrer">Yarah Bravo</a><br><a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://msplinks.com/MDFodHRwOi8vd3d3Lm15c3BhY2UuY29tL2dhYnJpZWx0ZW9kcm9z" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gabriel Teodros</a> w/ <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://msplinks.com/MDFodHRwOi8vd3d3Lm15c3BhY2UuY29tL2toaW5neg==" rel="noopener noreferrer">Khingz</a> &amp; <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315010005/http://msplinks.com/MDFodHRwOi8vd3d3Lm15c3BhY2UuY29tL3dkNGQ=" rel="noopener noreferrer">WD4D</a><br><br>8:00 PM :: 21+ w/ i.d.<br>Nectar (412 N. 36th St.)<br>Seattle, WA <br>$10 :: http://www.brownpapertickets.com/event/19359<br>http://www.obeseproductions.com<br><br>YOU DON'T WANNA MISS THIS SHOW!!!<br><br>Shouts out to the Hidmo,<br>daps1<br/></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></br></font><p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, He